    "question": {
      ":question/id": "72fe2234-ee62-52bd-b438-00b666155a09",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are in row echelon form.",
